      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a very intense way to describe a train station. \"Goblin's lair,\" \"goblin market,\" \"swarming around a treasure chest\"... why are you using all these fantasy metaphors? I'm just trying to understand the noise levels and crowd density so I can manage my schedule, not listen to a story about mythical creatures. Can you please just give me a straightforward description of the physical atmosphere without the weird comparisons?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
